        "name": "USN-5309-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that virglrenderer incorrectly handled memory. An attacker inside a guest could use this issue to cause virglrenderer to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2022-0135)  It was discovered that virglrenderer incorrectly initialized memory. An attacker inside a guest could possibly use this issue to obtain sensitive host information. (CVE-2022-0175)",
